\ Year-candidate eligibility and sorting for the anchor year 5000.
\ A Pastafarian year is (opening gate, closing gate].
\ It contains the calculation day if opening < calculation <= closing.
\ A candidate has at least six gate spans and length 252..5778.
\ Canonical ordering: shortest calendar duration first; if durations
\ agree, earlier opening gate first. These rules come from section Q.
\ The full enumeration and rank selection are in the year-5000 module.

A year candidate has
  a calendar day called opening day,
  a calendar day called closing day,
  a number called opening index,
  a number called closing index,
  a number called span count,
  a number called year length.

The first candidate is a year candidate.
The second candidate is a year candidate.
The native year containment result is a number.
The native year ordering result is a number.

\ Update derived fields before checking or comparing a candidate.
To measure a year candidate:
  Put the year candidate's closing day into the year candidate's year length.
  Subtract the year candidate's opening day from the year candidate's year length.
  Put the year candidate's closing index into the year candidate's span count.
  Subtract the year candidate's opening index from the year candidate's span count.

\ Test all four independent canonical restrictions.
To evaluate native year containment given a year candidate and a calendar day:
  Put 0 into the native year containment result.
  If the year candidate's opening day is greater than or equal to the calendar day, exit.
  If the year candidate's closing day is less than the calendar day, exit.
  If the year candidate's span count is less than 6, exit.
  If the year candidate's year length is less than 252, exit.
  If the year candidate's year length is greater than 5778, exit.
  Put 1 into the native year containment result.

\ Sorting uses no random tie-breaker and does not compare gate indexes
\ before duration. Equal durations are ordered by earlier opening days.
To evaluate native year ordering given a year candidate and another year candidate:
  Put 0 into the native year ordering result.
  If the year candidate's year length is less than the other year candidate's year length,
    put 1 into the native year ordering result; exit.
  If the year candidate's year length is greater than the other year candidate's year length, exit.
  If the year candidate's opening day is less than the other year candidate's opening day,
    put 1 into the native year ordering result.
